# Circuit Connections

## LDR Sensor Connections

The LDR and 10kΩ resistor form a voltage divider circuit for analog signal acquisition.

| Component            | Connection |
| -------------------- | ---------- |
| LDR Pin 1            | ESP32 3.3V |
| LDR Pin 2            | GPIO34     |
| 10kΩ Resistor Side 1 | GPIO34     |
| 10kΩ Resistor Side 2 | GND        |

### Voltage Divider Configuration

```text
3.3V
 |
[LDR]
 |
 +------ GPIO34 (Analog Input)
 |
[10kΩ]
 |
GND
```

---

# LED Connections

The LEDs display the 4-bit PCM encoded binary output.

| ESP32 GPIO Pin | Binary Bit | Connection                 |
| -------------- | ---------- | -------------------------- |
| GPIO18         | Bit0 (LSB) | GPIO18 → 220Ω → LED1 Anode |
| GPIO19         | Bit1       | GPIO19 → 220Ω → LED2 Anode |
| GPIO21         | Bit2       | GPIO21 → 220Ω → LED3 Anode |
| GPIO22         | Bit3 (MSB) | GPIO22 → 220Ω → LED4 Anode |

### LED Cathodes

All LED cathodes (short legs) are connected to:

```text
GND
```

